# The harbour's talk (the harbour's job, docs/systems/jobs.md): what its watch
# say when one hails another on his round (DistrictMap._hails: the pairs the
# rounds bring together), and what they say once a theft is found. Every line
# is yours to write: replace each <<...>>, keep the rest. A line carrying
# [note:<id>] teaches the player that pencil note (data/jobs/harbour.job) if
# he hears it: in 22 m, nothing solid between.

# The harbour's men (their posts), so a conversation can name them.
== cast
Rodrigo: sea_gate; swordsman
Tome: sea_gate; watchman
Duarte: quays; watchman
Inigo: quays; swordsman
Baltasar: customs; watchman
Leonor: carrack; duelist
Gaspar: tower; archer
Fernao: mole; watchman
Afonso: shipyard; brute

== harbour_tower_bell
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, at_ease
cast: A = name(Fernao); B = name(Gaspar)
cooldown: 4m
# intent: Fernao, at the golden tower's foot at the end of his round on the mole, calls up to the lookout; Gaspar answers from the terrace. Between them it comes out that the lookout has a bell, and rings it at anything amiss.
A: <<Fernao calls up to the tower>>
B [note:tower_bell]: <<Gaspar answers: the bell>>

== harbour_office_key
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, at_ease
cast: A = name(Baltasar); B = name(Duarte)|name(Inigo)
cooldown: 4m
# intent: The customs watchman and a quay lantern man at the customs house's door. It comes out that the office key is kept on the customs house's ground floor.
A: <<Baltasar hails the lantern man>>
B: <<the lantern man answers>>
A [note:office_key]: <<Baltasar: the office key, downstairs>>

== harbour_dark_bays
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, at_ease
cast: A = name(Duarte); B = name(Inigo)
cooldown: 4m
# intent: The two lantern men pass each other on the quays. Some of the Ribeira arcade's bays are left dark, and whoever finds a lamp out lights it again.
A: <<Duarte, passing>>
B [note:dark_bays]: <<Inigo: the dark bays, the lamps relit>>

== harbour_ways_up
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, at_ease
cast: A = name(Rodrigo); B = name(Tome)
cooldown: 4m
# intent: The two at the Sea Gate. The gate stays shut and watched at night; anyone going up takes the Guindais stair or the wall-walk.
A: <<Rodrigo, at the Sea Gate>>
B [note:ways_up]: <<Tome: the ways up at night>>

== harbour_cabin_key
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, at_ease
cast: A = name(Leonor); B = name(Duarte)|name(Inigo)
cooldown: 4m
# intent: The carrack's deck watch and a quay man at the gangway. The captain is ashore; he left his cabin key with the quay; his strongbox is in the cabin.
A: <<Leonor, from the deck>>
B: <<the quay man answers>>
A [note:cabin_key]: <<Leonor: the cabin key left on the quay>>

== harbour_theft_1
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, theft_noticed
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: once
# intent: After the theft is found: two of the watch, hunting, on what was taken.
A: <<after the theft: one>>
B: <<after the theft: the other>>

== harbour_theft_2
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, theft_noticed
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: once
# intent: After the theft is found: two of the watch on who could have done it, and how.
A: <<after the theft: one>>
B: <<after the theft: the other>>

== harbour_theft_3
where: harbour
when: situation:hail, theft_noticed
cast: A = any; B = any
cooldown: once
# intent: After the theft is found: two of the watch on what the harbourmaster will do to them.
A: <<after the theft: one>>
B: <<after the theft: the other>>
